***************************** T A L Y S **************************1725 1451  186
                                                                  1725 1451  187
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   1725 1451  188
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      1725 1451  189
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    1725 1451  190
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     1725 1451  191
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  1725 1451  192
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        1725 1451  193
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    1725 1451  194
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         1725 1451  195
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      1725 1451  196
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    1725 1451  197
stored in this data file:                                         1725 1451  198
                                                                  1725 1451  199
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   1725 1451  200
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     1725 1451  201
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 1725 1451  202
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   1725 1451  203
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                1725 1451  204
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   1725 1451  205
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    1725 1451  206
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        1725 1451  207
- Recoil data                                                     1725 1451  208
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           1725 1451  209
- Total particle energy spectra                                   1725 1451  210
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      1725 1451  211
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        1725 1451  212
- Residual production cross sections                              1725 1451  213
                                                                  1725 1451  214
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            1725 1451  215
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        1725 1451  216
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   1725 1451  217
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                1725 1451  218
                                                                  1725 1451  219
